[node:4a311aa7-5d33-43b6-be20-e3ab1fe53271]
type: decision
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/the-store-s-concurrency-rule-every-live
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:13:42.347956+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:271612ad-3d8e-4c9d-9464-33386852bac1] @ 2026-09-06T11:13:42.347956+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:2875ba91-ac6b-47d4-a382-d2aac85eac1d] @ 2026-09-06T11:13:42.347956+00:00

The store's concurrency rule: every live connection holds a SHARED file lock, and replacing the database file requires an EXCLUSIVE one (locking.py). Concurrency inside the file stays SQLite's job — shared locks do not serialize writers, and busy_timeout makes a contended commit wait. The lock is taken in MemoryStore.__init__, so it is opt-out rather than opt-in: every writer inherits it, including a script a future contributor writes without reading the docs. Chosen over routing all mutation through one server process, which would make a live server a precondition for writing and break the CLI's promise to work in a freshly cloned repo with nothing running.
---
