[node:775c666b-0637-412a-9bce-4c4744e5bd50]
type: constraint
tier: short-term
path: /artifact/when-the-exclusive-lock-cannot-be-taken
created_at: 2026-09-06T11:13:42.552429+00:00
needs_review: false
retrieval_weight: 1.0
trust_weight: 1.0
archived: false
-> HAS_FACET [node:271612ad-3d8e-4c9d-9464-33386852bac1] @ 2026-09-06T11:13:42.552429+00:00
-> DEPENDS_ON [node:4a311aa7-5d33-43b6-be20-e3ab1fe53271] @ 2026-09-06T11:13:42.552429+00:00

When the exclusive lock cannot be taken, the rebuild is skipped and reported, never performed anyway. The asymmetry decides it: a database that is merely out of date is visible in `agentic-memory sync status` and repaired by the next open, while a database swapped under a live connection is corrupt. The accepted consequence is that while the GUI server runs it holds the store open, so a `git pull` that moves the dump ahead is picked up only after the GUI stops.
---
